# The interface layer, on top of the project configuration one directory up.
#
# Qt owns its widgets through the parent pointer: `new QLabel(this)` hands the
# label to the parent, which deletes it. The check below assumes ownership is
# expressed with unique_ptr, and against a Qt widget tree it fires on every
# single construction, roughly fifty times in this directory alone. Silencing it
# per line would bury the code in comments and would still say nothing true, so
# it is turned off where the Qt idiom lives, and stays on everywhere else.
#
#   cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory
#     Widgets are owned by their parent, which is Qt's model and not a leak.

InheritParentConfig: true

Checks: >
  -cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory
